   "plugin": "Core",
   "model": "Notes",
   "data": {
    "text": "PERSONAL PLOT\nPatch any CV (0 to 10 V) into a jack. 0 V is the item's From setting, 10 V its To.\n\nCV-CC 1: MIDI channel 7, CC 33 to 48\n   1 Own plot weight\n   2 Own plot meets the main plot\n   3 What they want, against what they need\n   4 Secret\n   5 Closer to or further from the goal\n   6 Questions the audience is holding\n   7 A clock running out\n   8 Who knows first\n   9 What starts it all\n  10 Things get worse\n  11 The reversal\n  12 A choice with a cost\n  13 No going back\n  14 The other side makes a move\n  15 The forgotten plant\n  16 Showing the plan\nCV-CC 2: MIDI channel 7, CC 49 to 64\n   1 suite: Hidden agenda\n   2 suite: Chasing the wrong thing\n   3 suite: We know, they don't\n   4 suite: Bomb under the table\n   5 suite: Whodunit hook\n   6 suite: Two steps forward, one back\n   7 suite: The plan goes wrong\n   8 suite: Crossing the line\n   9 suite: Enemy closing in\n  10 suite: Heist caper\n  11 pair: When a secret starts slipping, cringe rises\n  12 pair: When the character is set back, their emotional road drops\n  13 pair: When a scene ends on a cliffhanger, the audience's questions rise\n  14 pair: When the opening grabs with a question, a question opens\n  15 pair: When the clock gets tight, the scenes speed up\n  16 pair: When the audience knows first, every calm moment fills with dread\nCV-CC 3: MIDI channel 7, CC 65 to 80\n   1 pair: When a side story grows heavy enough, it gets pulled into the main plot\n   2 pair: When a side story merges into the main plot, the stakes jump\n   3 pair: When what they want is the opposite of what they need, they fight the change\n   4 pair: When what they want finally lines up with what they need, they act on what they believe\n   5 pair: When something starts it all, the audience starts asking questions\n   6 pair: When they refuse the call twice, the stakes rise\n   7 pair: When things get worse, tension climbs\n   8 pair: When trouble lands just as it was going well, hope drops\n   9 pair: When the whole plan is told, it falls apart\n  10 pair: When the real plan is hidden, a reversal follows\n  11 pair: When things flip for the worse, the goal slips away\n  12 pair: When a choice costs a lot, the feeling is held in\n  13 pair: When a choice can never be undone, there is no going back\n  14 pair: When there is no going back, the stakes rise\n  15 pair: When the other side moves, dread grows\n  16 pair: When we see the other side's move, we know first\nCV-CC 4: MIDI channel 7, CC 81 to 94\n   1 pair: When the other side is at the door, things get worse\n   2 pair: When a plant is well hidden, the reveal is bigger\n   3 pair: When the clock is down to seconds, the cuts speed up\n   4 pair: When the talk loosens up, a secret slips out\n   5 pair: When the plan is laid out in full, something is bound to go wrong\n   6 pair: When it all seems to fall apart, the hidden part of the plan pays off\n   7 pairs: Secrets and lies\n   8 pairs: Questions pull the audience forward\n   9 pairs: Knowing too much\n  10 pairs: The side story takes over\n  11 pairs: Plan to pieces\n  12 pairs: The line crossed\n  13 pairs: Enemy at the door\n  14 pairs: Heist caper: the moves"
   },
